From fc94e4ad4114bd25adacf4b5f6e3c51de4a18a7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:26:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] TASK-260830-uqnwmi:
 prove-record-version-and-union-closure

Add the record-level conformance sweep for the six dimensions the pinned
v0.5.0 specification declares over an authoritative record and that no
single-shape test establishes:

- round trip: Canonicalize is idempotent and identity-preserving for every
  registered shape, does not launder a malformed member across a self-ID
  recomputation, and the fixture digests are pairwise distinct;
- unknown field: the same reverse-DNS key is refused at the top level and
  accepted under extensions, binding both halves of the Section 1.5 boundary;
- historical major: every v0.4.3 Section 1.5 contract version is retained by
  the v0.5.0 registry, the detector is a pure function with its own dropped
  and additive negative proof, the historical projection is proven not to be
  the current one, and every historical-major fixture is accepted at the
  identity entries while an unregistered future major is refused;
- enum union closure: every closed-vocabulary position of every fixture is fed
  the union of every other pinned vocabulary and must refuse everything outside
  its own declared set, with per-position sets derived from the pinned
  inventory and four genuinely ambiguous positions carrying a reviewed
  resolution that must remain one of the candidate rows;
- provenance: every Section 10.1 record family drives its four envelope members
  absent, null, wrongly typed, empty, and carrying a right-typed value in the
  wrong identity grammar, with the absent case pinned to the closed member set
  that actually refuses it;
- cross-record reference: one coherent session lineage resolves every reference
  through a content-addressed store keyed by recomputed digest, and a
  substituted same-schema, same-subject record must not resolve.

Reuses the existing derived machinery - the fixture inventory, the pinned
closed-vocabulary artifact, the total-refusal and registered-validator
derivations - rather than hand-listing any set. In-object couplings stay owned
by the existing coupling inventory and are not restated.

Audited by a recorded mutation run over the production sources: five mutants
are refused by these tests, one is refused by the existing coupling inventory
that owns its clause, and one is documented as an equivalent mutant subsumed by
requireExactMembers with that subsumption pinned in the sweep itself.

Change-Request: TASK-260830-uqnwmi
